Batch 4: Incline Traversal, Camps & Environment (Messages #83 – #135)


[#83 – #90] Uphill Sprint Jitter Diagnosis




User: Noted that when sprinting uphill, the feet were smooth but the body was jittery.


Resolution: Diagnosed the 27 Hz Pelvis Jackhammer. The code was using Math.min(footL, footR) to set hip height. On steep slopes, the trailing foot dropped 0.5m every stride, violently shaking the spine.


Fix: Decoupled pelvis height from individual feet. Pelvis follows a smooth ground-center trajectory with an athletic forward lean into the slope; two-bone leg IK absorbs all elevation reach. Leg IK is completely bypassed during swimming, climbing, and ragdoll.






